              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "турбаза (turbáza) — \"a holiday camp, a tourist centre\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Летом мы отдыхали на турбазе у озера. Létom my otdykháli na turbáze u ózera. In summer we stayed at a holiday camp by the lake."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine; short for туристическая база: simple cabins in the countryside."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "турбаза (turbáza) is a short form of туристическая база 'a tourist base', from турист 'a tourist' and база 'a base'. EtymDB lists база and турист without a source; турист is usually traced through French touriste and tour to Latin tornāre 'to turn on a lathe' (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
